{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of IPv4 ICMP redirects on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final reboot test shows persistent zero-valued settings for all, default, and eth0, with live accept_redirects=0 on every observed scope (all, default, eth0, and lo). The changed boot identity and restored network/SSH health directly demonstrate persistence through restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-19a1cf58d0b34167","cmd-6cc269751efd4f9f","cmd-9adfde712c894ae7","cmd-f64d3c46b75b42a1","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of IPv4 source-routed packets on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final reboot test shows persistent zero-valued settings for all, default, and eth0, with live accept_source_route=0 on every observed scope. The post-restart checks also show recovered addressing, routing, gateway reachability, and SSH.","evidence_ids":["cmd-19a1cf58d0b34167","cmd-6cc269751efd4f9f","cmd-9adfde712c894ae7","cmd-f64d3c46b75b42a1","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic are observed before and after the work. The implementation used the platform's existing sysctl/init facilities, with no package installation or upgrade evident and package health remaining consistent.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ae7dcd163f504eee","cmd-19a1cf58d0b34167","cmd-f64d3c46b75b42a1","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Editing /etc/sysctl.conf and applying live values directly implemented the hardening; the first reboot revealed a genuine legacy eth0 boot-order defect, the eth0-specific correction resolved it, and the second reboot supplied final persistence and mandatory restart evidence. The retained pre-change sysctl backup has a clear rollback role rather than being unexplained residue. Temporary reboot logging was absent from the final /tmp inventory. No package-health degradation, new exposure, or conflicting service residue was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3c1f0f97bb354151","cmd-b917ab4b85994cbb","cmd-81467a530ecd43ed","cmd-52d99d84e32c4fd4","cmd-6cc269751efd4f9f","cmd-f64d3c46b75b42a1","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The final provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: it records a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity, and recovered hardening, networking, gateway reachability, and SSH. The lifecycle boot identity independently matches the final post-restart observation.","limitations":["Failed-service comparison was unavailable because systemctl is unsupported on this legacy release; recovered SSH and network behavior were checked directly instead.","The lifecycle after-prepare boot identity predates an earlier diagnostic reboot, so it does not equal the final protocol's pre-restart identity; the chronological command evidence explains this intermediate boot and the after-executor identity matches the final post-restart identity."]}
